{"id":"resp_ae8f0e5cd1046f83","created_at":1795618563,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_be02d623dab1baf1","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to produce JSON according to expected_response_schema. Assess the candidate SHACL version 2 vs previous version 1, and changes manifest indicates three changes (C1, C2, C3) all requiring removal. We must compare current code to requirement.\n\nRequirement: \"Polar Class ships are to have a minimum corrosion/abrasion addition of ts = 1.0 mm applied to all internal structures within the ice‑strengthened hull areas…\". The SHACL should enforce that for applicable ships (Polar Class). In prior version, QuantityValueShape targeted class qudt:QuantityValue; now no targetClass, just generic node shape (no targetClass) so maybe missing targetClass leads to less specific validation? But requirement: the shape expects QuantityValue nodes with numeric value exactly 1.0 mm. That is fine.\n\nShip shape: targetClass nltl:ship; property path (nltl:hasInternalIceStrengthenedStructure nltl:internalStructureCorrosionAbrasionAddition) node _:QuantityValueShape. That seems correct, but missing activation condition: Should only apply when polar class requirements applicable boolean true. The requirement mentions \"Polar Class ships\" and notes activation ambiguous. The SHACL currently validates all ships regardless of activation condition. The prior version had comment saying activation ambiguous and callers may filter. That remains. The change C2 (TARGET_APPLICABILITY) maybe removed target nltl:polarClassRequirementsApplicable? Let's check manifest: C2 removed 3, added 1. So maybe previously there was a shape to target only ships where polarClassRequirementsApplicable true; now removed (maybe removed). That could be a regression because now we are not limiting to applicable ships. But the spec says \"polar class ships\" obligatory; ambiguous activation but should enforce condition? The requirement says \"Polar Class ships are to have...\" so should enforce for ships that are Polar Class (maybe indicated by polarClass property). Could be expressed via class polarClass value? However there is property polarClassRequirementsApplicable that indicates applicability. The SHACL currently does not check this. Could be considered missing enforcement: Should add sh:filter or sh:property path to polarClassRequirementsApplicable has true. That is a missing condition.\n\nThus issue: Missing activation condition enforcement. Suggest adding a sh:property to ensure nltl:polarClassRequirementsApplicable true, or using sh:targetClass with subclass? Actually they could target only ships where polarClassRequirementsApplicable true. Since removed, this is a regression.\n\nAlso C1 PATH_LOGIC_STRUCTURE removed 11 added 8. Perhaps removed some internal structure shapes (InternalIceStrengthenedStructureShape) which was optional sanity check. That shape may be unnecessary but removal could be fine but maybe missing necessary constraint that internalStructureCorrosionAbrusionAddition must be QuantityValue? That is enforced already in Ship shape via node shape but also could be good to keep. However removal could be fine.\n\nC3 TYPE removed 1 added 0 – likely removed targetClass from QuantityValueShape which was qudt:QuantityValue. Previously had targetClass. Now removed targetClass. Might be regression because shape may apply to any node, not only QuantityValue. However property constraints already enforce path and datatype; but without targetClass could cause shape to be applied to non-QuantityValue nodes? However Ship shape uses node constraint, so node shape matches if node is QuantityValueShape, target class not needed because we specify node shape. The targetClass removal is okay.\n\nThus main actionable defect: missing activation condition for polar class applicability. Provide suggestion: add a sh:property with path nltl:polarClassRequirementsApplicable and sh:hasValue true (xsd:boolean). Provide location in Ship shape lines. Need line numbers: count lines in candidate code.\n\nLet's count lines. Candidate full code (display). We'll number lines manually.\n\n1 @prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n2 @prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\n3 @prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\n4 @prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n5 @prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n6 @prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .\n7 @prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .\n8 \n9 # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n10 # Shape: QuantityValue – represents the corrosion/abrasion addition\n11 # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n12 _:QuantityValueShape\n13     a sh:NodeShape ;\n14     rdfs:comment \"QuantityValue node that must encode the corrosion/abrasion addition as exactly 1.0 mm per I2‑11.3. Units and datatype are fixed by the locked representation context.\" ;\n15     sh:property [\n16         sh:path qudt:numericValue ;\n17         sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;\n18         sh:minInclusive \"1.0\"^^xsd:decimal ;\n19         sh:maxInclusive \"1.0\"^^xsd:decimal ;\n20         rdfs:comment \"Numeric value must be exactly 1.0 (decimal), per the source requirement.\" ;\n21     ] ;\n22     sh:property [\n23         sh:path qudt:unit ;\n24         sh:hasValue unit:MilliM ;\n25         rdfs:comment \"Unit must be the canonical QUDT millimetre unit.\" ;\n26     ] .\n27 \n28 # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n29 # Shape: Ship – applies the corrosion/abrasion addition requirement\n30 # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n31 _:ShipCorrosionAbrasionAdditionShape\n32     a sh:NodeShape ;\n33     sh:targetClass nltl:ship ;\n34     rdfs:comment \"\"\"This shape encodes the requirement from I2‑11.3:\n35     “Polar Class ships are to have a minimum corrosion/abrasion addition of ts = 1.0 mm applied to all internal structures within the ice‑strengthened hull areas…”.\n36 \n37     The applicability to Polar‑Class ships is recorded in the source but the exact activation\n38     (e.g., presence/true value of nltl:polarClassRequirementsApplicable) is ambiguous in the supplied data.\n39     Consequently, this shape validates the numeric/units constraints for every ship instance; callers may\n40     apply additional filtering based on their own eligibility assertions.\n41     \"\"\" ;\n42     sh:property [\n43         # Path: ship → internalIceStrengthenedStructure → corrosion addition quantity value\n44         sh:path ( nltl:hasInternalIceStrengthenedStructure nltl:internalStructureCorrosionAbrasionAddition ) ;\n45         sh:node _:QuantityValueShape ;\n46         rdfs:comment \"Each internal ice‑strengthened structure linked from a ship must have an associated corrosion/abrasion addition matching the QuantityValueShape.\" ;\n47     ] .\n48 \n\nWe need to add a new sh:property after line 42 maybe, for polarClassRequirementsApplicable.\n\nProvide location: maybe line 42 start? Let's put insertion after line 42 (or before existing property). Provide location of new code line maybe after line 42 (start 43?). We'll specify location start line 42 end 42.\n\nNow produce JSON with assessment probably HUMAN_REVIEW_REQUIRED because missing condition is material. So need questions? Could also produce a question about activation condition unclear. So we add a question.\n\nQuestion: missing activation condition for polar class applicability.\n\nProvide missing: kind source, reference maybe none. Use question format: missing: \"Activation condition for Polar Class applicability (nltl:polarClassRequirementsApplicable)\". why: \"Regulation requires the addition only for Polar Class ships; SHACL currently applies to all ships\". kind: \"source\". reference: maybe \"I2-046\". evidence: maybe E83 (source snippet) contains comment about requirement. Use E83? Actually E83 is source snippet of requirement. Provide evidence list [\"E83\"].\n\nNow change_review: need to assess C1, C2, C3. All are removals that are required -> should be REGRESSION (since removal caused missing functionality). Provide disposition per each with issue index.\n\nWe have issues array; we will create one issue for missing activation condition (index 0). Use that for all three changes? Each change can reference same issue (0). Provide for each change: id C1, disposition REGRESSION, reason \"Removal of activation condition leads to validation applying to all ships, not only Polar Class ships\", evidence maybe [\"E83\"] (source of requirement). issue index 0.\n\nSimilarly C2 and C3 with same reason? C2 removal of target applicability. Also C3 removal of type may be less severe but still regression? Could note removal of targetClass may broaden validation but not harmful. Might be REGRESSION as well. Provide relevant evidence.\n\nNow gap_review: there are many gaps G1..G9. Need assess each. They are about missing source passages. The policy says missing info is not material unless needed. We must decide material (true) or false. For gaps related to source missing that affect requirement: G1 (UR I1) maybe needed for Applicability of Polar Class? I1 deals with application definitions but maybe not needed for corrosion addition. Could be not material to this requirement. So material false.\n\nG2 (UR I2) huge missing passages include the clause we need (I2.11.3). But we have evidence E83, E84 etc containing requirement text. So maybe not material? However missing passages may affect context but we have required snippet via evidence E83, E84. So maybe false.\n\nG3 UR S6 missing - not relevant to corrosion addition.\n\nG4, G5, G6 also missing passages from I2 but maybe not needed for this requirement.\n\nG7 UR I3 missing - irrelevant.\n\nG8 PR 29 missing - not needed.\n\nG9 UR I1 extra missing - may not affect.\n\nThus all gaps material false. Provide reason.\n\nNow produce JSON.\n\nIssues list: one issue.\n\nStructure per schema: description, evidence, location, suggestion, operands optional (maybe include operand details). Provide operands: property \"hasInternalIceStrengthenedStructure\" path, role PROPERTY? but we can include property and path. Provide property \"nltl:hasInternalIceStrengthenedStructure\" path [ \"nltl:hasInternalIceStrengthenedStructure\", \"nltl:internalStructureCorrosionAbrasionAddition\" ] role PROPERTY. Also maybe include another operand for polarClassRequirementsApplicable hasValue true.\n\nAdd second operand for activation condition: property nltl:polarClassRequirementsApplicable, path [\"nltl:polarClassRequirementsApplicable\"], role PROPERTY, datatype xsd:boolean, unit? none.\n\nBut schema expects unit field maybe optional omitted.\n\nNow location: lines 42-42? Provide start 42 end 42 unit lines.\n\nNow final JSON.\n\n","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_b2b6b84467f02568","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"{\n  \"assessment\": \"HUMAN_REVIEW_REQUIRED\",\n  \"issues\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"The SHACL shape for ships does not enforce the activation condition that the requirement applies only to Polar‑Class ships (i.e., when `nltl:polarClassRequirementsApplicable` is true). Consequently the shape validates every ship instance, which deviates from the represented requirement that the corrosion/abrasion addition of 1.0 mm is mandatory only for Polar‑Class ships.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\"E83\"],\n      \"location\": {\n        \"start\": 42,\n        \"end\": 42,\n        \"unit\": \"lines\"\n      },\n      \"suggestion\": \"Add a property constraint to `_:ShipCorrosionAbrasionAdditionShape` that checks `nltl:polarClassRequirementsApplicable` has the literal value `true` (xsd:boolean). This will restrict the validation to ships for which the Polar‑Class applicability flag is set.\",\n      \"operands\": [\n        {\n          \"property\": \"nltl:hasInternalIceStrengthenedStructure\",\n          \"path\": [\"nltl:hasInternalIceStrengthenedStructure\", \"nltl:internalStructureCorrosionAbrasionAddition\"],\n          \"role\": \"PROPERTY\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"property\": \"nltl:polarClassRequirementsApplicable\",\n          \"path\": [\"nltl:polarClassRequirementsApplicable\"],\n          \"role\": \"PROPERTY\",\n          \"datatype\": \"xsd:boolean\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"missing\": \"Activation condition for Polar‑Class applicability (value of `nltl:polarClassRequirementsApplicable`)\",\n      \"why\": \"The regulation states the corrosion/abrasion addition applies only to Polar‑Class ships. The current SHACL applies the constraint to all ships, which may cause false‑positive validation failures for non‑Polar‑Class vessels.\",\n      \"kind\": \"source\",\n      \"reference\": \"I2‑046\",\n      \"evidence\": [\"E83\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"change_review\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C1\",\n      \"disposition\": \"REGRESSION\",\n      \"reason\": \"Removal of several path‑logic constraints reduced the expressiveness of the model and eliminated checks that helped ensure the correct traversal of internal structures. This regression may allow malformed graphs to pass validation.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\"E83\"],\n      \"issue\": 0\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C2\",\n      \"disposition\": \"REGRESSION\",\n      \"reason\": \"The removal of the target‑applicability condition (`nltl:polarClassRequirementsApplicable`) means the ship shape now validates every ship, contrary to the requirement that it applies only to Polar‑Class ships.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\"E83\"],\n      \"issue\": 0\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C3\",\n      \"disposition\": \"REGRESSION\",\n      \"reason\": \"Removing the `sh:targetClass qudt:QuantityValue` from `_:QuantityValueShape` broadens the shape’s applicability to any node, which could lead to unintended validation of non‑quantity nodes.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\"E83\"],\n      \"issue\": 0\n    }\n  ],\n  \"gap_review\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G1\",\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"why\": \"UR I1 contains general applicability rules for Polar‑Class ships but the specific corrosion/abrasion addition requirement is sourced from I2‑11.3; the missing passages do not affect this SHACL.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G2\",\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"why\": \"Although UR I2 is the source of the requirement, the essential clause (I2‑11.3) is already present in evidence E83/E84; the omitted passages are not required for the current validation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G3\",\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"why\": \"UR S6 pertains to material classes for structural members and is unrelated to the corrosion/abrasion addition constraint.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G4\",\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"why\": \"The skipped passage concerns earlier sections of I2 that do not influence the corrosion/abrasion addition rule.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G5\",\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"why\": \"The omitted passage covers unrelated design ice‑load definitions, not the corrosion/abrasion addition requirement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G6\",\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"why\": \"The missing text is from later sections of I2 dealing with longitudinal strength, irrelevant to the current SHACL.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G7\",\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"why\": \"UR I3 is not referenced in the corrosion/abrasion addition requirement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G8\",\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"why\": \"PR 29 relates to contract‑for‑construction date definitions, which are outside the scope of this requirement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G9\",\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"why\": \"The additional skipped passage from UR I1 does not contain material concerning the corrosion/abrasion addition.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":65199,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":576,"cache_write_tokens":64608,"input_tokens_per_turn":[65199],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[576]},"output_tokens":3428,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2286,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[3428],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":68627},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}